Both StatusWatermarkValve and CombinedWatermarkStatus derive watermarks and deal with idle inputs (from input channel or input split respectively). However, cases where all inputs are marked as idle are handled differently. In both cases, the maximum watermark should be derived from all idle inputs.

From comments in StatusWatermarkValve (which implements this already):
{code}
// now that all subpartitions are idle and no subpartitions will continue to advance
// its watermark, we should "flush" all watermarks across all subpartitions;
// effectively, this
// means emitting the max watermark across all subpartitions as the new watermark.
{code}

