in 2015, this issue was already created, and closed soon after with reason "workaround, move to linux". It is occurring only on Windows, and only when doing "spark-submit" in "--master local[*]" (default) mode , which is admitedly a very rare case for real usages.

It appears that it give a very bad image of spark while teaching it to students who are mostly working on windows, and learning how to use "spark-submit" mode.

The root cause of the bug is that on windows, you can not delete a directory if there are still locked (=opened) files in it, and the temporary copy of the jar is indeed still locked by the Executor classLoader  

When you do
{noformat}
C:> spark-submit  --class %MY_CLASS%  "submitted-app.jar"
{noformat}

Internally, because it is "local[*]" mode, spark JVM has internally (>=) 2 classLoaders, 
- 1 classLoader for the "driver" part that points to the "submitted-app.jar" file given in argument (this file is OK, the directory is not touched), 
- 1 classLoader for the "executor" part, that points to a copy of the jar in a created temporary directory "C:\Users\<username>\AppData\Local\Temp\spark-<uuid>\submitted-app.jar".... This file causes the error at stop time.

The fix to it is simply to call the Executor URLClassLoader.close() method when everything else is already closed for the Executor, to really close correctly all files ressources.
This is in class Executor, accessible by "defaultSessionState.urlClassLoader"

{noformat}
diff --git a/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/executor/Executor.scala b/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/executor/Exeutor.scala
index f1087b695..23bf4ad06 100644
--- a/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/executor/Executor.scala
+++ b/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/executor/Executor.scala
@@ -467,6 +467,8 @@ private[spark] class Executor(
       if (!isLocal) {
         env.stop()
       }
+      logInfo("close Executor classLoader")
+      defaultSessionState.urlClassLoader.close(); // cf [SPARK-12216]
     }
   }
{noformat}

